✔ [Phase 1 - Existing-System Audit and Reusable Contracts] Define the boundary between generic hotkey-group infrastructure and feature-specific group definitions. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Inventory the responsibilities currently combined in `dwarfui/ui_hotkeys.lua` and `dwarfui-ui-hotkeys.lua`: @done(26-07-31 16:55)
        - native element discovery,
        - rectangle validation and layout signatures,
        - semantic button ordering,
        - DF binding lookup and label normalization,
        - snapshot caching,
        - bounded overlay layout and rendering.
    ✔ Document the current public exports and preserve compatible entry points for `UiHotkeyModel` and `UiMenuHotkeysOverlay` during migration. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Define a generic `HotkeyGroupDefinition` contract containing a stable group ID, activity provider, layout provider, button definitions, and label-placement configuration. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Define a canonical `HotkeyGroupLayout` result containing the group bounds, semantic element bounds, and a provider-owned layout signature. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Define a generic `HotkeyButtonDefinition` contract containing a stable semantic ID, DF action binding, and element selector. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Define immutable public enums for closed configuration concepts such as geometry source kind and label anchor. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Define failure behavior for inactive, missing, incomplete, and ambiguous groups without allowing one failed group or button to suppress unrelated labels. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    ✔ Confirm that discovery providers are read-only and never manipulate the OS pointer or synthesize mouse clicks. @done(26-07-31 16:55)
    Deliverables:
    - Approved LuaDoc contracts for group definitions, layouts, elements, buttons, and snapshots.
    - Compatibility inventory for the existing UI-hotkey model and overlay exports.
    - Explicit ownership rules for generic infrastructure versus concrete group definitions.
    Decisions:
    - Generic semantics are joined to discovered geometry by stable `element_id`, never inferred from coordinates.
    - Layout providers own source-specific signatures and return typed inactive, unavailable, or ambiguous outcomes.
    - Native structures, widget containers, rendered signatures, and custom adapters share one validated layout boundary.
    - Provider discovery is strictly read-only; input simulation is not a geometry-discovery mechanism.
    - `UiHotkeyModel`, `UiMenuHotkeysOverlay`, their current snapshot fields, and `dwarfui-ui-hotkeys.ui_hotkeys` remain compatibility surfaces.
    Docs:
    - `Docs/reusable-hotkey-groups-contract.md`

✔ [Phase 2 - Generic Geometry Primitives] Extract reusable rectangle and rendered-element discovery utilities. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Add `dwarfui/hotkeys/geometry.lua` as a reload-managed production module. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Implement validated rectangle construction, copying, union, containment, equality, and screen-to-local translation helpers. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Implement configurable connected-component sampling over a caller-provided screen region. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Implement repeated-strip extraction that derives group position, element width, element height, and element rectangles from sampled native geometry. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Make search regions, expected element counts, candidate validation, and element ordering caller-provided instead of bottom-toolbar constants. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Generate stable geometry signatures from actual group and element bounds so same-resolution movement invalidates caches. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Reject ambiguous candidate sets instead of silently selecting an arbitrary component. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    ✔ Ensure rendered overlay labels cannot permanently corrupt subsequent native-layout detection. @done(26-07-31 17:02)
    Deliverables:
    - Generic geometry module with no fortress-mode, bottom-bar, or Citizens-specific behavior.
    - Deterministic geometry fixtures covering adjacent elements and competing native components.
    Decisions:
    - Geometry APIs operate on caller-provided inclusive rectangles and tile readers; the module has no knowledge of a particular viewscreen or toolbar.
    - Repeated strips are accepted only when exactly one candidate satisfies the configured axis, count, and validators; ambiguity returns an explicit error code.
    - Element ordering is spatial and deterministic; semantic meaning remains the responsibility of later group definitions.
    - Geometry scans are stateless and never retain sampled cells or mutate input, so transient overlay labels cannot poison future scans.
    - `HotkeyStripAxis` is an immutable public enum, and all returned rectangles are copied and validated at module boundaries.
    Docs:
    - `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/hotkeys/geometry.lua`
    - `tests/hotkey_geometry.spec.lua`

✔ [Phase 3 - Reusable Layout Providers] Support native-structure, widget-tree, and rendered-signature sources through one layout contract. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Add `dwarfui/hotkeys/layout_provider.lua` with the common provider interface and result validation. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Implement a rendered-strip provider backed by the generic geometry primitives. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Allow rendered providers to supply a search-region provider, component validator, semantic element ordering, and layout-signature data. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Implement a native-control provider that accepts a feature-specific callback for locating native structures or widget roots and extracting their rectangles. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Support native widget traversal only when the located object is a `df.widget_container`; do not assume all native controls are widgets. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Allow custom providers to adapt other exposed native screen structures without changing the generic model. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    ✔ Validate all provider results at the module boundary and suppress invalid layouts safely. @done(26-07-31 17:12)
    Deliverables:
    - Interchangeable rendered-strip and native-control provider implementations.
    - A provider test double suitable for deterministic model and overlay tests.
    Decisions:
    - Providers are plain callable adapters; `invoke` contains exceptions and validates every returned rectangle, group ID, element map, and signature.
    - Rendered providers delegate scanning and ambiguity handling to `HotkeyGeometry`, while definitions supply search, candidate, ordering, and signature callbacks.
    - Native providers call widget traversal only after an explicit `df.widget_container` test; all other located values use a feature-specific extractor.
    - Native and rendered adapters share the same canonical layout boundary, allowing custom native structures without generic-model changes.
    Docs:
    - `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/hotkeys/layout_provider.lua`
    - `tests/hotkey_layout_provider.spec.lua`

✔ [Phase 4 - Generic Hotkey Group Model] Move binding resolution, caching, and snapshot construction into a reusable model. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Add `dwarfui/hotkeys/model.lua` containing `HotkeyGroupModel`. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Accept a `HotkeyGroupDefinition` and injectable dimensions, tile-reading, binding, and activity collaborators. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Resolve active key displays by converting named actions through `df.interface_key` before calling DFHack key-display APIs. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Move compact label normalization into the generic hotkey subsystem. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Cache geometry by the provider-owned layout signature while resolving active bindings independently of geometry-cache changes. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Map semantic button definitions to provider elements without coupling the model to visual position. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Return a canonical snapshot containing group bounds, resolved buttons, active state, and layout signature. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Clear all cached geometry immediately when the group becomes inactive. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    ✔ Preserve per-button suppression when either geometry or a binding is unavailable. @done(26-07-31 17:25)
    Deliverables:
    - Reusable `HotkeyGroupModel` with injectable providers and no concrete toolbar catalog.
    - Compatibility adapter or specialization retaining the existing `UiHotkeyModel` entry point.
    Decisions:
    - The model invokes providers each snapshot to observe same-resolution movement, but retains validated geometry while the provider signature is unchanged.
    - Binding labels are resolved on every snapshot and normalized after the named action is converted through `df.interface_key`.
    - Semantic definitions join provider elements by `element_id`; visual ordering is never inferred by the model.
    - Inactive, unavailable, and ambiguous layouts clear cached geometry immediately; missing geometry or labels suppress only that button.
    Docs:
    - `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/hotkeys/model.lua`
    - `tests/hotkey_model.spec.lua`

☐ [Phase 5 - Generic Bounded Overlay] Implement reusable rendering for independently positioned hotkey groups.
    ☐ Add `dwarfui/hotkeys/overlay.lua` containing a reusable `HotkeyGroupOverlay` base class.
    ☐ Accept a model builder and configurable label anchor, inset, and pen.
    ☐ Fit each overlay frame to the current resolved group bounds instead of allocating a fullscreen host.
    ☐ Render through the overlay body painter using overlay-local coordinates derived from screen-space element bounds.
    ☐ Re-layout when the group moves or changes size, including changes that preserve the screen resolution.
    ☐ Collapse safely to an inert minimal frame when the group is unavailable.
    ☐ Keep keyboard and pointer input fully pass-through.
    ☐ Support multiple independently registered group overlays without shared mutable geometry or lifecycle state.
    Deliverables:
    - Reusable bounded overlay base class.
    - Test fixture demonstrating two independent hotkey groups with different positions and layouts.

